# What a protected AWS install accepts in the management grants its stack defines.
#
# A grant to the management identity from a permission set the stack defines (one that is not the
# built-in set of its id) may name only actions this file covers. A grant that could reach any
# other action is refused when it is rendered, so a wildcard such as `iam:*`, `cloudformation:*`
# or `*` fails instead of being filtered. The built-in permission sets are reviewed separately.
#
# Format: `action <IAM action pattern>  # reason`. A requested pattern is covered when this
# file's pattern matches it with the requested pattern's own `*` and `?` taken as literal
# characters, so `s3:Get*` covers `s3:GetObject` and `s3:Get*Tagging` but not `s3:*`.
# Every line needs a reason. Add a line only for an action that cannot change what runs,
# change an identity or its permissions, or reach what only setup or the verifier may write.

# Reads
action *:Get*                    # reads; no read changes a resource
action *:List*                   # reads
action *:Describe*               # reads
action *:BatchGet*               # reads
action dynamodb:Query            # reads items by key
action dynamodb:Scan             # reads items

# Data in the install's own storage
action s3:PutObject              # writes an object; a bucket's policy and ACL are other actions
action s3:DeleteObject           # deletes an object
action s3:AbortMultipartUpload   # ends an upload the caller started
action dynamodb:PutItem          # writes an item
action dynamodb:UpdateItem       # updates an item
action dynamodb:DeleteItem       # deletes an item
action dynamodb:BatchWriteItem   # writes items
action dynamodb:ConditionCheckItem  # checks an item inside a transaction

# Messages
action sqs:SendMessage           # sends a message
action sqs:ReceiveMessage        # receives a message
action sqs:DeleteMessage         # deletes a received message
action sqs:ChangeMessageVisibility  # delays a received message
action sqs:PurgeQueue            # empties a queue; its policy is another action
action sns:Publish               # publishes a message
action events:PutEvents          # puts an event on a bus

# Telemetry
action logs:CreateLogStream      # creates a stream inside a log group
action logs:PutLogEvents         # writes log lines
action cloudwatch:PutMetricData  # writes metric points

# Encryption with a key the install already has; a grant on a key is another action
action kms:Encrypt              # encrypts data
action kms:Decrypt              # decrypts data
action kms:GenerateDataKey*     # makes a data key
action kms:ReEncrypt*           # re-encrypts data

# Calling what the release signed
action lambda:InvokeFunction    # runs the function as released; its code and configuration are other actions
action execute-api:Invoke       # calls an API Gateway route as released
